{"kind":"report","text":"Rules 16 room (d8d9f465): the three routes compared, plus a fourth. Recommendation: (1), a dap-lending switch with sc_psbin3zi… kept installed. It takes two heads and one deployment window.\n\nA gap in every hosted route: the upgrade cohort is not admitted by default. `deploymentCreationDefaults()` (packages/platform/src/version-relations.ts:128) holds the base, failed-claim, archive-device-publication, unpublished and commons cohorts only. dap-lending's PLATFORM_CREATION_PINS adds register@5/directory@5 and others, but not register@29, directory@28 or rules@16. So the Worker would refuse the install even with REGISTER_SCOPE set. The pins must change in a reviewed head before the window.\n\n(1) dap-lending, both roots installed.\n- Head P, before the window, full gate:\n  - apps/room/wrangler.lending.jsonc PLATFORM_CREATION_PINS gains platform:register@29, platform:directory@28 and platform:rules@16. Membership 14, Destination 21 and Inbox 1 are already there.\n  - REGISTER_SCOPE stays sc_psbin3zi…, so nothing changes for live rooms.\n  - You deploy P.\n- The window, as in cutover plan 036. The plan expires 14 min after `--plan` (docs/cli.md:122), and no gate fits in 14 min.\n  1. Run `dap install --plan … --cohort upgrade` in a new empty home.\n  2. Within the window, deploy main's tracked lending file with --var REGISTER_SCOPE=\u003cnew register\u003e, ARTIFACTS_CONFIG.registerScope=\u003cnew register\u003e and INSTALLED_REGISTER_SCOPES=[\"\u003cnew register\u003e\",\"sc_psbin3zi…\"].\n  3. `dap install --planned`, then `dap create`.\n  Listing the old root keeps its creation policy (head A note, 2026-11-14), so old rooms keep base-cohort children. Child creation, Git host authority (ruling 3b239919, docs/deploy.md INSTALLED_REGISTER_SCOPES) and archive-host-item.ts:32 all read the installed list. dap-lending has no archive bridge setting.\n- Head Q, after the window, full gate: `node scripts/register-values.mjs lending --keep --register \u003cnew\u003e --genesis \u003cnew genesis\u003e` syncs the tracked file. Until Q lands, never run `deploy.mjs lending`, because it would restore the single old root. This is the same rule as after the cutover window.\n- Checks after the window, before any witness:\n  - Child creation: one app install in counter-witness from its operator home. Counter declares no prefix, and the room already holds many items. This adds one item of residue.\n  - Clone: `dap clone` from the lending-library and lending-shelf operator homes. It reads the Git token through host authority under the old root.\n  - Publication: lending-library publishes one shelf page, or you name a cheaper write.\n  - `dap verify --all` in each of the three old homes.\n  - The DO rate read after the deployment.\n- Residue: one register and one room on dap-lending, and a two-root Worker until a later --only head retires a root.\n\n(2) dap-demo: the same mechanics. The demo's Browser Start creates visitor rooms under the current register, so a switch changes what every public visitor gets: Rules 16 rooms, an unreviewed onboarding change. dap-demo also already carries the cutover's single-root history. Not recommended.\n\n(3) The self-hosted laptop kit: no screens until SH-1. It can witness the Counter upgrade through the CLI and MCP only, and it cannot witness LS-7 at all. Not recommended for LS-7. A fallback for U4's CLI half only.\n\n(4) Not in your list: a dedicated Worker whose only register is upgrade-cohort, as O4 ran on its own Worker. It puts no live room at risk and needs no two-root period. But it needs a new wrangler file, DO and Artifacts namespaces, SESSION_SECRET, a deploy-policy entry, a rate-baseline row, SCREEN_HOSTS rows with a new roomOrigin, and the same 14-min window for its first REGISTER_SCOPE. It costs more than (1). Choose it only if you do not accept any two-root risk to the three live dap-lending rooms.\n\nRecommendation: (1). dap-demo ran two installed roots from 6 to 14 Nov (Register 26 with 17 kept), so the multi-root path has been live before. The upgrade cohort differs from base only in Register 29, Directory 28 and Rules 16. Head P and head Q are mine: P is small, and Q is the generated register-values sync. The window is yours. With your word I file P now, after the U4 marker gate ends, because no second gate runs beside it.","body":{"to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}